I've twice been down to the castle, and twice not found the WOW.  The first
time I searched every square I could get to without luck.  I found the
square in the tower with Elbereth burned into the ground, but apart from
thst it was empty!

The second time I got there I quaffed a Potion of Object Detection and plainly
saw where the WOW was.  I went around to the back door and then quaffed
another PoOD, and to my annoyance the WOW was gone!  Entered into the
castle and wiped out everything, no WOW!  What gives!!

(Also the Armour and Weapon store rooms guarded by the Dragons turned out
to be mostly empty when I got there, and it wasn't the Dragons that had
picked it up either.  (PoOD showed these rooms as full.)

I've noticed two facts, the first I would consider a bug.
When searching for a hidden door, monsters suddenly become aware of the
door as soon as you do (for example at the back door of the castle I could
see with telapethy that all the monsters were waiting just inside the door
(*none* fell through any of the 4 trap doors - another problem).  I walked
around behind the Castle for a while leting the monsters wait.  About 50
turns later I searched and found the door, and lo and behold the monsters
on the other side of the door sudenly found the door and came out at me!
This does not seem reasonable.

The second is to do with Potion of Object Detection, I cant reliably say this
but it does seem that other monsters on the same level become more aware of
random trasure once the player has taken a PoOD.  At one stage when I was
copying save files I found that doing a level with and without PoOD made a
difference to the objects being picked up by monsters.  (I tried this a few
times each way, but I'm not 100% sure of this yet.)

BTW, not a gripe.  I found an alternative to getting past the 4 trap doors
in the Castle over Boots of Levitation/Potion of L, I used a scroll of taming
and a leash.  I'll leave the rest of it as something for the reader to
figure out.

